<title>FRANCE: French Robien job sparing law &quot;stupid&quot; - Pasqua.</title>
<headline>French Robien job sparing law &quot;stupid&quot; - Pasqua.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's &quot;Robien law&quot;, designed to protect jobs in private firms through payroll charge relief for employers who reduce working hours, is &quot;completely stupid&quot;, Gaullist RPR party heavyweight Charles Pasqua said on Monday.</p>
<p>Pasqua, who does not hold a ministerial post in the RPR-UDF government colation, told a lunch meeting of the Anglo-American Press Association that work-sharing was not a panacea.</p>
<p>&quot;It makes me scream when I see work sharing presented like some sort of panacea,&quot; he said. &quot;The Robien law is totally stupid.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5453</p>
</text>
